<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/MudBlazor/MudBlazor.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>
<body>
    @* No @rendermode at the Routes level — each @page declares its own. Login
       stays SSR (so its form post can set the auth cookie); every other page
       declares @rendermode RenderMode.InteractiveServer and is rendered through
       MainLayout, which itself opts into interactive mode so MudBlazor's
       providers and the page components share the same circuit. *@
    <Routes />
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
    <script src="_content/MudBlazor/MudBlazor.min.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
